            <ArticleTitle>[A woman with abdominal pain, nausea and vomiting].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A6566</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 82-year-old female came to the emergency department because of abdominal pain, nausea and vomiting. Physical examination was suggestive of ileus. CT imaging of the abdomen showed a sciatic hernia. Familiarity with this rare pelvic floor herniation is essential for making the diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
